<title>UK: Sedgwick nine month pre-tax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Sedgwick nine month pre-tax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>				   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  9.8		    vs 10.2</p>
<p> Pretax			 80.4		   vs 76.5</p>
<p> Brokerage and fees	 690.7		  vs 655.0</p>
<p> Investment/other income  33.5		   vs 37.0</p>
<p> Operating profit	   84.0		   vs 82.9</p>
<p> Expenses		    640.2		  vs 609.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 77.0 to 78.6 million stg.  </p>
<p> Tax		    26.5		 vs 20.3</p>
<p> Interest payable   7.7		  vs 10.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Insurance broker Sedgwick Group Plc said the industry wide reduction in insurance rating levels affected most parts of its business.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
